#show: handout.with(
  title: [Argumentative Essay Rubric],
  subtitle: [Scoring guide with four criteria and four performance levels],
  subject: [English Language Arts],
)

#student-info("name", "date", "score")

#v(0.5em)

Use this rubric to score each criterion from 4 (Excellent) down to 1 (Beginning). The total is out of 16.

#rubric(
  levels: ([Excellent], [Proficient], [Developing], [Beginning]),
  points: (4, 3, 2, 1),
  (
    [Thesis and claim],
    [The thesis is clear, specific and arguable. It takes a definite position and guides the whole essay.],
    [The thesis is clear and arguable, but it is somewhat general or only partly guides the essay.],
    [The thesis is present but vague, or it states a topic rather than a position.],
    [The thesis is missing or unclear, or the essay does not take a position.],
  ),
  (
    [Evidence and reasoning],
    [Strong, relevant evidence from credible sources supports every claim. Reasoning is logical, and counterarguments are addressed and rebutted.],
    [Relevant evidence supports most claims. Reasoning is mostly logical, and a counterargument is acknowledged.],
    [Evidence is limited, general or only loosely connected to the claims. Reasoning has gaps, and counterarguments are barely mentioned.],
    [Evidence is missing or irrelevant. Claims are unsupported, and there is no counterargument.],
  ),
  (
    [Organization],
    [The introduction, body and conclusion are well developed. Paragraphs are focused, and transitions make the argument easy to follow.],
    [The structure is clear. Most paragraphs are focused, and transitions are generally effective.],
    [The structure is uneven. Some paragraphs lack focus, and transitions are few or abrupt.],
    [The structure is hard to follow, with little paragraphing or logical order.],
  ),
  (
    [Language and conventions],
    [The style is precise and persuasive, and the tone is suitably formal. There are almost no errors in grammar, spelling or punctuation.],
    [The language is clear and mostly formal. A few errors do not get in the way of meaning.],
    [The language is sometimes unclear or informal. Errors are frequent and occasionally distract the reader.],
    [Frequent errors make the essay hard to understand.],
  ),
)

#v(1em)

